<title>HUNGARY: HUNGARY OCT PRELIM. C/A GAP $40MLN VS SEPT $38MLN.</title>
<headline>HUNGARY OCT PRELIM. C/A GAP $40MLN VS SEPT $38MLN.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's current accound</p>
<p>deficit widened by $40 million in October, compared with $38</p>
<p>million in September, the National Bank of Hungary (NBH) said</p>
<p>in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p>HUNGARY C/A BALANCE (in million dollars)</p>
<p>    OCT 96	 SEPT 96	JAN-OCT 96   JAN-OCT 95</p>
<p>    -40	     -38	    -1,144	 -2,156</p>
<p>NOTE - Hungary's current account target for 1996 is $2 billion. The NBH said that Hungary continued to have a large surplus in the balance of tourism revenues/expenditures in October. The net outflow of revenues from the country and the amount of interest paid on debt by Hungary decreased in October, while the month's trade deficit was almost the same than November's, the NBH added.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
</text>
